      en: "The Mesarya Plain (Mesaoria) is the central lowland of Cyprus, spanning from Nicosia to Famagusta Bay. It is the island's agricultural heartland, producing wheat, barley, potatoes, and citrus. The plain is flat and low-lying, with an average elevation of 50 m. Historically, it was a battleground for invading armies. It is now densely populated and hosts the capital Nicosia. The plain is formed by alluvial deposits from the Troodos mountains.",
